<title>UK: RUSSIAN BANK EYES ROSNEFT OIL CO - FT REPORT.</title>
<headline>RUSSIAN BANK EYES ROSNEFT OIL CO - FT REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The president of the Russian bank Oneximbank, Vladimir Potanin, aims to try and acquire the last major state-owned oil company in Russia when it is privatised later this year, said the Financial Times on Friday.</p>
<p>The FT report, based on an interview with Potanin, said the banking boss believed the oil group Rosneft would fit in with existing interests.</p>
<p>The sale of Rosneft could raise more than $1 billion.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717.</p>
</text>
